{
  "dom_id": "step-e4408",
  "name": "Example: Multiplying a Matrix by the Identity Matrix",
  "problem": "Calculate the product $I_3 B$ given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]$",
  "worked_solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
